# playpick gave mode=battleground map=escort spec=druid:guardian style=mash
# view=1280x800 save=carried. #7 in direction.md has one tank-spec mash pull
# on record (2026-09-27-19, conquest, fresh) and it lost eighteen seconds
# faster and 110 points worse than a dps-mash pull on the same map -- the
# argument being that mash never leaves its pull spot (no steer term in
# scripts/playbot.ts) so parking the team's only tank there, rather than an
# interchangeable dps, costs more. Escort has never seen mash at all (six
# prior sessions: dodge x2, melee x2, wander x2) and never seen a tank spec
# either (the one tank on this map, 2026-09-29-something paladin:protection,
# was melee-style). This is the second tank-mash battleground pull ever, on a
# different map, matched on viewport (1280x800 desktop) to the first -- worth
# seeing whether "losing the tank specifically is worse" holds on a map whose
# whole win condition is a moving cart rather than a held point.
open
targets
shot front

tap battleground
tap map:escort
targets
shot escort-picked

tap class:druid:guardian
tap pull
waitscreen fight 15
shot pulled
state
targets

play mash 100
shot mid1
state
bill

wait 5
play mash 100
shot mid2
state
bill

wait 5
play mash 100
shot mid3
state
bill
says
targets
